eryjoery/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeryjoery/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeryjoery/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joeryjoery","id":22054219,"login":"joeryjoery","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMDU0MjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeryjoery/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeryjoery/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeryjoery/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeryjoery/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeryjoery/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeryjoery","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"NONE","body":"> Thanks for the report. I think this is working as expected: the new key data type is not recognized by numpy, so you will not be able to use it with numpy functions.\r\n> \r\n> We understand that some downstream libraries are not yet compatible with the new key types; this is the reason we have not yet switched over to recommending the new-style universally (e.g. all the JAX docs still recommend `jax.random.PRNGKey` at this point).\r\n\r\nI see, thanks for clarifying. I thought this was unintentional.\r\n","created_at":"2023-12-02T09:37:31Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/18767#issuecomment-1837104137","id":1837104137,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18767","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5tf_wJ","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1837104137/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-12-02T09:37:31Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1837104137","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2205